2026-11-07T06:56:27.9509690Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9537870Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9538890Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9539720Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9540060Z 
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9540350Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9540650Z 
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9540930Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9541840Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9542020Z 
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9542180Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9542470Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9542620Z 
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9542880Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T06:56:27.9543270Z   $ sh ./install-nix
